#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:38
msgid "`--input` / `--report` / `-i`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:40
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Repeatable, and takes several values after one occurrence. Each value is "
"a **document specifier** in the `<url>:<path>:<name>` grammar — "
"{doc}`../../guides/user/documents` is that grammar in full, including how"
" a `:` inside a value is quoted and what `save_pdf` does in each case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:49
msgid ""
"Giving none from this source leaves the field **unset** rather than "
"empty, so a configuration file or the environment can still supply the "
"documents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:52
msgid "`--format` / `-f`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:54
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The format name, as `metadata/formats.csv` of the repository synthesises "
"it — `EURIZON-EN23`, `FINECO-EN23@LUX`, `MEDIOLANUM-IT24.A`. It is "
"optional: left out, each job settles its format from its own documents. "
"{doc}`../design/document-classification` explains why the run works this "
"way; this section is what it does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:59
msgid "Where the format comes from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:61
msgid ""
"A job settles its format after its documents are resolved and before the "
"format's recipe is loaded, from three sources in a fixed priority:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:64
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**the configuration** — `-f`, or `format` from any other source "
"({doc}`../configuration/options`);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:65
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**the document classification** — the repository's "
"`metadata/document_classify.yaml` and Python module ({doc}`../formats"
"/document-classify-yaml`, {doc}`../formats/document-classify-python`), "
"applied to the first pages of each document;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:68
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**the URL** — the repository's `url_mapping.csv`, applied to the URL of "
"each document that has one: the longest matching prefix wins, then the "
"row with the more specific name, then the row that comes first. A row may"
" give a partial name ({doc}`../formats/names`), which narrows the format "
"without settling it; another source then has to complete it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:73
msgid ""
"The classification **runs even when the format is configured**: that is "
"how the run can tell you that the format you gave is not the one the "
"document looks like. It costs roughly 0.1–0.2 s per job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:76
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The two document sources are combined exactly as `freeports classify` "
"combines them ({doc}`freeports-classify`, \"How the two sources "
"combine\"): two names agree when some format of the repository falls "
"under both, and the result is the most precise name both allow. The "
"documents of one job are combined source by source first, then the two "
"sources compared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:81
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The job runs only with a **complete** format. A partial one — "
"`MEDIOLANUM-IT24.*`, say — fails the job, and the error lists the formats"
" it still allows; run `freeports classify` on the document, or see "
"{doc}`../formats/names`, to choose one, then give it with `-f`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:85
msgid "When the sources cross"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports.md:87
msgid ""
"Every crossing is logged once per job, at the level below. The `WARN` "
"lines are not something a setting can switch off, and since `.log.csv` "
"always records `WARN` and above, they are there even under `-qq`."
msgstr ""

